  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-10-25 (dev 2399d5ad7c; owner-requested re-check of the 17 actionable open P2 violated INV/META items; fixtures archived under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/premise_check_10252026/). VERDICT: PARTLY FIXED; title re-scoped to `logs`. Code read only (ci-debug not run: network). `status` and `cron-status` now address a leg: gate selection substring-matches a leg context such as nightly/2, and `ci-debug cron-status` (scripts/ci-debug:382-415, a72d4808f4, INV-bozid) lists each leg with its own URL and step verdicts. `logs` still cannot: the resolver is _github_fetch_job_log in scripts/lib/github-api.sh:272 (NOT in scripts/ci-debug); _wp_pipeline_coords (:163-175) parses the workflow index off target_url -- its comment says that index is what a matrix leg's context points at -- and the log path DISCARDS it at :402 (`read -r wp_repo wp_pipeline _`), flattens every workflow's steps (:416-417) and returns the first failing step or steps[-1] (:433). The per-step reader _wp_render_steps (:242-246) already filters by workflow index. PREMISE CORRECTION: the description guessed the four statuses share one target_url, leaving nothing to disambiguate with; by the code's own contract each leg URL carries /<workflow index> and the fetcher throws it away, so the fix is to pass the parsed index through, not to invent a discriminator (not verified against a live status payload). GOVERNANCE NOTE: scripts/lib/github-api.sh is not on the AGENTS.md governance list (only scripts/ci-debug and scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh are). NOT checked: the byte-identical-log evidence, the --actions arm (WI-pubur)."  # c664
